With the approval of Premier Li Keqiang, the State Council recently issued the "Decision on further reducing the catalogue and simplifying the approval process for the management of production licenses for industrial products."
The "Decision" proposes to further reduce the production license management catalogue of industrial products, cancel the management of production licenses for 14 types of industrial products, and decentralize the management authority of production licenses of 4 types of industrial products to the quality and technical supervision departments of the people's governments at the provincial level.
After this reform, the implementation of industrial product production license management products will be reduced from last year's 38 categories to the current 24 categories.
The "Decision" makes it clear to implement a simplified approval process for products within the catalogue.
The first is to change the pre-certificate product inspection organized by the issuing authority to the product inspection and qualification report issued by the enterprise at the time of application by a qualified inspection and testing institution.
Second, in addition to hazardous chemicals, the provincial people's government quality and technical supervision departments (market supervision and management departments) to carry out on-the-site review of licensed products, enterprises submitted applications and product inspection qualified reports and made a commitment to ensure product quality and safety, through the form of examination can receive production licenses, and then subject to on-site review within the prescribed time.
In accordance with the principle of â€œone enterprise and one certificateâ€ , when applying for a new license or applying for a new license, a license shall be issued together.
The "Decision" requires that all regions and relevant departments should solidly promote the reduction catalogue and simplify the approval process.
Strengthen the commitment of enterprises to publicize and on-site review, strengthen credit supervision and binding means, implement the main responsibility of enterprise quality, and revoke production licenses for false promises and non-compliance with requirements.
For products that cancel the production license management of industrial products, it is necessary to earnestly strengthen post-event supervision, involving public health and safety, environmental protection and other products can be converted into mandatory certification, a positive list is listed and announced to the public, a unified certification standard, a reasonable reduction and certification testing project, mandatory certification costs are in principle borne by finance at all levels according to the system.
Take support measures to encourage enterprises to carry out voluntary certification to promote the establishment of brands and the expansion of the market.
It is necessary to benchmark international advanced standards and promote the improvement of industrial product quality.
Give full play to the role of third-party social organizations to ensure the quality and safety of industrial products.
For products that retain the production license management of industrial products, it is necessary to improve the standard system, give full play to the advantages of industry supervision, strengthen the responsibility of "who approves and who supervises", dynamically evaluate product quality and safety risks, timely reduce the catalogue, decentralize the approval authority, or turn into certification management.
In September, China's comprehensive PMI month-on-month, the manufacturing PMI rebounded month-on-month.
According to the data released by the National Bureau of Statistics of China on the 30th, China's comprehensive PMI output index was 54.1% in September, higher than the previous month and the annual average of 0.3 and 0.1 percentage points, indicating that the production and business activities of Chinese enterprises have generally remained stable.
In the same month, the manufacturing production index and non-manufacturing business activity index, which constitute the comprehensive PMI output index, were 53.0% and 54.9%, respectively, a month-on-month increase.
Among them, China's manufacturing PMI was 50.8%, down 0.5 percentage points month-on-month.
Zhao Qinghe said that there are five main characteristics of this month's manufacturing PMI:
First, the fundamentals of the manufacturing industry are generally stable.
Among the 21 industries surveyed, the PMIs of the 14 industries are in the expansion range, of which the manufacturing PMIs of pharmaceuticals, special equipment, electrical machinery and equipment are located at a higher operating level of more than 53.5%, and the growth rate is faster.
The second is a small fluctuation between supply and demand.
The production index and the new orders index were 53.0% and 52.00%, respectively, down 0.3 and 0.2 percentage points from the previous month, and supply and demand continued to maintain a stable state, but the expansion slowed down slightly.
The new export order index and the import index were 48.0% and 48.5%, respectively, down from 1.4 and 0.6 percentage points in the previous month, and the prosperity fell to the lowest point of the year.
The fourth is to increase the cost of purchasing raw materials for enterprises.
The main raw material purchase price index was 59.8%, an increase of 1.1 percentage points from the previous month, and the ex-factory price index was 54.3%, the same level as the previous month and the highest point in the year.
Fifth, the operation of large-scale enterprises is stable, and the operating conditions of small enterprises continue to improve.
Large enterprise PMI was 52.1%, the same as the previous month, this year the index has always been in an expansion range of 52.0% and above this year, and this month's production index and the new orders index have increased month-on-month, which is the main driving force for the manufacturing industry to maintain the expansion; the PMI of medium-sized enterprises was 48.7%, lower than 1.7 percentage points in the previous month, located in the contraction range.
In the same month, China's non-manufacturing business activity index was 54.9%, an increase of 0.7 percentage points from the previous month, rising for two consecutive months.
Zhao Qinghe believes that the non-manufacturing industry as a whole continues to maintain a steady and good development momentum.
The business activity index of road transportation, securities, real estate and other industries continues to be below the critical point, and the total volume of business has decreased.
Nagoya, Nov 5 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan (PBOC) Governor Haroda said on Monday that the central bank’s awareness of a long-term ultra-loose monetary policy could squint the profit margins of financial institutions and could destabilize the country’s banking system.
However, he said the BOJ needed to maintain its large-scale stimulus package, given sluggish inflation and fraught economic uncertainty abroad, while keeping a close eye on the pros and cons of its policies.
â€œThe Bank of Japan fully recognizes that the strength of financial institutions will be increasingly affected in the face of continued monetary easing,â€ Kuroda said in Nagoya's speech to corporate leaders.
He said that if financial institutions are more active in undertaking risks to compensate for the impact of narrowing profit margins caused by low interest rates for many years, the banking system is likely to turbulence in the event of a serious negative impact.
â€œAlthough these risks are not high at this time, the central bank will pay close attention to the development of the situation and encourage financial institutions to take the necessary measures,â€ he said.
Minutes of the Bank of Japan’s meeting, released earlier on Monday, showed that at a meeting in September, the bank’s policy committee discussed the rising costs of long-term easing.
According to the minutes of the meeting, a member of the committee said that if the economy continues to expand, "the Bank of Japan will have more room for flexibility in terms of policy in the future."
According to the records of the meeting, another member said that in view of the limitations of the duration of the policy, the committee should discuss how long the Bank of Japan can maintain the stimulus policy.
Kuroda said that the Bank of Japan will assess the financial risks caused by the easing policy, but also need to take into account the uncertainty surrounding Japan's economic prospects, due to Sino-US trade frictions and rising protectionism, which may affect global demand.
â€œThe impact of such problems on Japan's economy will be limited for the time being,â€ Kuroda said.
â€œBut if the problem persists, the impact on Japan’s economy is likely to get bigger,” he added.
â€œThere is a need for a sustained and robust monetary easing while considering positive and negative impacts in a balanced manner,â€ Kuroda said.
While the drawbacks of aggressive stimulus programs, such as prolonged low interest rates eroding the profits of financial institutions, sluggish inflation has forced the Bank of Japan to maintain it.
The Bank of Japan maintained monetary policy last month; in the face of the risks posed by the global trade war dispute, Kuroda has ruled out the possibility of raising interest rates in the near future.
On June 1, 2018, the United States Cardiff, the corporate logo on Tesla's electric vehicles.
According to a settlement agreement, U.S. Tesla Motors and its CEO Musk have each agreed to pay $20 million in fines to financial regulators, and Musk will also step down as the company's chairman, but remain CEO.
The settlement agreement will put an end to two months of turmoil for Tesla.
The settlement of the securities fraud allegations disclosed by the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission on Saturday will give investors a sigh of relief.
Investors were worried that a protracted legal battle would only go a further blow to the still-losing electric car company.
The SEC on Thursday sued Musk for fraud, saying its Aug. 7 tweet misled investors.
The tweet said that he is considering taking Tesla private for $420 per share and has received financing.
The SEC said that the tweets were virtually unsubstantiated and that the market turbulence they triggered hurt investors.
Investors and corporate governance experts said the agreement could strengthen Tesla, which has been hit hard by Musk’s recent actions.
Steven Heim, the head of Boston’s Common Asset Management, said the settlement should put Musk under more oversight, without taking “devastating” measures to drive him out of Tesla.
The asset management firm holds shares in Tesla’s battery maker Panasonic.
According to this proposed agreement, Tesla must appoint an independent chairman, two independent directors, and a committee of directors to formulate controls on Musk's external communication.
â€œIt is in the best interests of our market and for our investors, including Tesla shareholders, to resolve this matter quickly, in accordance with the agreed terms,â€ SEC Chairman Clayton said in a statement.
Thursday’s allegations wiped out about $7 billion in Tesla’s market value, which was $45.2 billion on Friday, down from GM’s $47.5 billion.
In the settlement agreement, the SEC rescinded the request to remove Musk from the company's leadership.
Many investors said the penalty would be catastrophic.
â€œI think this is the best possible outcome for everyone involved,â€ said Ivan Feinseth of Tigress Financial Partners, which gave Tesla a â€œNeutralâ€ rating and called the SEC penalty a â€œlight penaltyâ€ for Musk.
â€œHe’s still CEO is very important to Tesla.â€
Neither Musk nor Tesla acknowledged or denied the SEC’s allegations in the settlement, nor did they immediately respond to a request for comment.
The settlement agreement still needs to be approved by the court.
Beijing Morning News (Reporter Wang Ping) The Beijing Morning Post reporter recently learned from the Beijing Construction Industry Group that one of the core architectural groups of the 2019 Beijing World Garden Association Park, the Beijing World Garden Performing Arts Square project will adopt the multi-color ETFE puzzle film structure for the first time, and the film structure of 5,440 square meters will present six kinds of colors of deep red, dark green, orange, blue, red and green.
According to Liu Changbao, the project leader of the Beijing Construction Engineering Five Construction Group, the performance square project construction area is 4,500 square meters, with a total amount of 1182 tons of steel installed, and the steel structure roof is supported by the cantilevered steel truss, which shows the shape of the "butterflies wings" under the tens of thousands of quilts.
â€œLooking at the performing arts square from the middle of the air, the colorful roof is like a colorful butterflies through flowers and dancing, and the bright colors don't gradually fascinate due to the passage of time and wind, rain and snow.â€
Previously, the monochromatic ETFE membrane structure has been widely used in bird's nest, water cube and other projects, but the multi-color puzzle ETFE membrane structure is still the first in the country.
The reporter learned that there are very few global suppliers with a variety of color film structure production capacity, so every inch of membrane structural material is very "precious".
Liu Changbao said that in order to avoid problems such as overlap and "fights" at the end of the cable end position, it will also innovatively adopt the "dual-for-ear" cable head structure to ensure that the "fights" of the rope head is in the right place.
At present, the construction of the 2019 Beijing World Park Park is under way.
Among them, the international pavilion project has completed the hoisting construction of all "flower umbrellas".
It is planned that the project will be equipped at the end of October.
Overseas Chinese around the world celebrate the 69th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China
On the occasion of the 69th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China, overseas Chinese held a variety of festivities and jointly wished the motherland better in the future.
On the evening of the 23rd local time, the Association of Australian Chinese Groups invited more than 500 compatriots and friendly people to gather in Sydney.
The guests admired the superb performance of the Chinese artists, and expressed their family feelings.
Wu Changmao, chairman of the Chinese Association, said that China's rapid progress and development have made the sons and daughters of China who are overseas feel proud.
2018 coincides with the 200th anniversary of the arrival of Chinese people in Australia, and overseas Chinese will continue to carry forward 200-year-old fine traditions, integrate more actively into the mainstream society, be a strong bond of friendship between China and Australia, and make unremitting efforts for the economic development and social progress of the two countries.
On the same day, the Botswana China Association for the Promotion of Peaceful Reunification and the Chinese Charitable Foundation, the Overseas Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Botswana and the Gaborone Chinese Aid Center jointly held the "2018 Overseas Chinese Association" in Gaborone.
At the fraternity meeting, the compatriots showed their "housekeeping skills".
There is a deep chorus of hymns for the birth of the motherland.
The President of the General Chamber of Commerce of Overseas Chinese in Botswana and director of the Gaborone China Aid Center, said that while adhering to the traditional virtues of the Chinese nation and realizing the dream of life, the overseas Chinese communion has also contributed to the prosperity of Botswana and won the respect of the local people.
He called on overseas compatriots to grasp the precious opportunities provided by the development of the motherland, set sail in the new era, and make new contributions.
In the past few days, China's foreign institutions have held National Day receptions.
On the evening of the 24th local time, the Chinese ambassador to Thailand Lu Jian held a reception in Bangkok.
Representatives of overseas Chinese, Chinese-funded institutions, volunteer teachers and international students, well-known people from all walks of life in Thailand and foreign diplomatic missions in Thailand attended.
The guests at the meeting shared Chinese food, and the atmosphere was warm and friendly.
On the evening of the 26th local time, at the reception of the Chinese Consulate General in Los Angeles in Los Angeles, jointly sponsored by the Consulate-General and the China News Agency, the "Film Forward: 40 Years of China's Reform and Opening-up Photo Exhibition" was held at the same time.
The exhibition captures the historical moments of China's reform and opening-up process from 1978 to 2018, showing the great achievements of reform and opening up and the development of Sino-US relations.
"I have been in the United States for 38 years, see so many wonderful and historic pictures, the mood is very excited."
Zhang Xianghua, a Chinese-American entrepreneur and philanthropist, said that the achievements of China's reform and opening up are "remarkable", and as a Chinese, he is very proud.
Liu Yuanji, a “post-90s” who works in Los Angeles, said that most of the recorded photos occurred before he was born and did not know it.
â€œSlowly in chronological order, I feel that China is taking it step by step and becoming more and more powerful, which makes us particularly excited in foreign countries,â€ Liu Yuanji said.
Many overseas Chinese are not far away and return to China to participate in the festivities.
On the evening of the 27th, the 2018 "Cultural China and Global Chinese Concert" was played at the National Theatre in Beijing, and overseas compatriots were invited.
Under the guidance of Chinese in Italy and the artistic director of the National Grand Theatre Lu Jia, the classic repertoire was staged successively, and under the familiar melody and high-level interpretation, the overseas compatriots were irritated.
There are more people who have traveled through the mountains of the motherland.
Since the beginning of September, thousands of kilometers have been flying 30,000 kilometers in 26 days, from the westernmost to the easternmost part of China, spanning 15 cities in six provinces and 15 cities.
"My motherland is a vast country and a great world, which is one of the brightest pearls on the face of the earth!"
On October 1, Zhang Tao returned to Dubai due to official duties.
Abe intends to let Ganli serve as a key position of the Liberal Democratic Party cabinet reshuffle and other discussions come to an end -Zhongxin.com
According to Japan's Kyodo News Agency on October 1, Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe entered the final stage of discussion for the cabinet reshuffle on the 2nd and the adjustment of the party's high-level personnel.
It is currently in the process of co-ordinating the election countermeasures committee or the chief executive chairman or chairman of the election response committee for the four key positions of Abe's cronies.
According to reports, the relevant personnel of the regime disclosed the above information on the 1st.
In the afternoon, Abe held a meeting at his official residence with the head of the Kuomintang Party, Yamaguchi.
Yamaguchi demanded that land and transportation from the Gongming Party be allowed to remain in office.
Abe said, "It will be discussed."
Yamaguchi disclosed the matter to the media.
At noon on the 1st at the official residence of the Liberal Democratic People's Party (LDP), Abe met with the vice president of the Liberal Democratic Progressive Party (LDP) Takamura and called for "hope to continue to provide help in the future" on the revision of the Constitution.
Takamura currently serves as a special adviser to the party's headquarters for the advancement of the constitution.
It is reported that as the promoter of "Abenomics", Ganli served as an economic regeneration minister in December 2012, when the second Abe's cabinet came to power, but resigned in January 2016 due to a money scandal.
He served as the head of the party's presidential election headquarters.
Focusing on the party's four key positions, Abe intends to let the director-in-charge, second-ranking Junbo, and the chairman of the government affairs investigation, Kishida Wenxiong, continue to serve.
The general chairman, who is responsible for summarizing the discussions within the party related to the revision of the Constitution and directing the selection of the chairman in next year's Senate election has become the focus.
With regard to the cabinet, it has been basically decided to maintain the backbone of political regimes such as Deputy Prime Minister Taro Aso and Chief Cabinet Secretary Suga Yiwei.
Ishii has served as the chairman of the Kuomintang party and government, etc., first served as a cabinet member in a cabinet reshuffle in October 2015 and served for about three years.
On the morning of the 2nd, Abe will decide high-level personnel at the general meeting of the Liberal Democratic Party.
According to the plan, the list of cabinet ministers will be announced in the afternoon, followed by a certification ceremony at the Royal Palace.
SHANGHAI, Sept. 30 (Reuters) - The China Securities Regulatory Commission on Sunday officially released the revised Guidelines for the Governance of Listed Companies, which focus on further strengthening restrictions on controlling shareholders, actual controllers and their related parties, paying more attention to the protection of small and medium-sized investors and giving full play to the role of small and medium-sized investor protection institutions, while actively drawing on international experience to promote the participation of institutional investors in corporate governance.
The CSRC pointed out that the revised guidelines cover the basic concepts and principles of the governance of listed companies, the composition and operation of the shareholders' meeting, the board of directors and the board of supervisors, the rights and obligations of directors, supervisors and senior managers, the incentive and restraint mechanism of listed companies, and the behavioral norms of controlling shareholders and their related parties.
The new standards also include the participation of institutional investors and related institutions in corporate governance, the basic requirements of listed companies in terms of stakeholders, environmental protection and social responsibilities, and information disclosure and transparency.
The revised guidelines require listed companies to implement the development concepts of innovation, coordination, greenness, openness and sharing in corporate governance, increase the party building requirements of listed companies, and strengthen the leading role of listed companies in environmental protection and social responsibilities.
Strengthen the role of the Board’s audit committee and establish a basic framework for environmental, social responsibility, and corporate governance (ESG) information disclosure.
In addition, in response to the concerns of all parties, the new standards also put forward new requirements for the stability of control faced by listed companies in the governance of listed companies, the performance of independent directors, the high evaluation and incentive restraint mechanism of directors and supervisors of listed companies, and the strengthening of information disclosure.
In accordance with the new guidelines, we will study and improve the relevant regulations and normative documents, guide self-regulatory organizations such as the stock exchanges and the China Association of Listed Companies to formulate and modify relevant self-regulatory rules, and gradually improve the governance rule system of listed companies.
At the same time, we should strengthen the training of listed companies, strengthen the consciousness of listed companies to improve their governance and standardized operation, and continuously improve the quality of listed companies.
Chinese President Xi Jinping said on Monday that China's opening-up door will not be closed will only get bigger and bigger, and the pace of promoting a higher level of opening-up will not stop.
The expansion of imports is not a measure of equity, it is a long-term consideration facing the future, and it is expected that in the next 15 years, China's imports of goods and services will more than 30 trillion US dollars and 10 trillion US dollars, respectively.
Xi Jinping delivered a keynote speech at the 1st China International Import Expo, China will further reduce tariffs, accelerate the development of new formats such as cross-border e-commerce, continue to relax market access, promote the opening up of the service industry, the domestic market has a large gap in education, medical and other fields will relax foreign equity restrictions.
China will protect the legitimate rights and interests of foreign-funded enterprises.
He pointed out that China will study and put forward the policy and institutional system of Hainan's step-by-step construction of a free trade port, accelerate the process of exploring and building a free trade port with Chinese characteristics; it will add a new area of the Shanghai Free Trade Zone; set up a scientific and technological innovation board on the Shanghai Stock Exchange, and test the registration system to support the regional integration and development of the Yangtze River Delta and rise to a national strategy.
“China’s economy is a sea, not a small pond.
"When the wind is calm, there is also a strong storm," Xi Jinping said, "the tempest and rain can overturn small ponds, but can't overturn the sea.
There have been a lot of storms, and the sea is still there!
After more than 5,000 years of hardship, China is still there!
Facing the future, China will always be here!"
He pointed out that economic globalization has suffered setbacks, multilateralism and the free trade system have been affected, there are still a lot of unstable and uncertain factors, and risks and challenges have intensified; open cooperation is an important driving force to enhance international economic and trade cooperation, and all countries should adhere to openness and integration, expand the space for mutually beneficial development, and strengthen macroeconomic coordination.
He once again stressed that China's open door will not be closed, it will only get bigger and bigger, and the pace of promoting a higher level of opening-up will not stop.
China will stimulate the potential of imports, comply with the upward trend of domestic consumption, take more active and effective measures to promote the increase of residents' income, and cultivate medium and high-end consumption growth points.
China will respect international business practices and treat all types of enterprises registered in the territory of China without discrimination and equality.
China will protect the legitimate rights and interests of foreign-invested enterprises, resolutely punish violations of the legitimate rights and interests of foreign investors, especially the infringement of intellectual property rights in accordance with the law, improve the quality and efficiency of intellectual property examination, introduce a punitive compensation system, and significantly increase the cost of violations.
Talking about China's economic prospects, Xi Jinping said that China's economic operation is in a reasonable range from the perspective of major indicators such as economic growth, employment, prices, balance of payments, corporate profits, fiscal revenue, and labor productivity, which lays an important foundation for achieving the goals and tasks for the whole year.
Compared with the other major economies, China's economic growth is still among the highest in the world.
"China's healthy and stable fundamentals of economic development have not changed, the production factor conditions to support high-quality development have not changed, and the overall momentum of long-term steady improvement has not changed."
Xi Jinping said that for China's economic development prospects, we can be very optimistic.
Xi Jinping said that China's macro-control capacity has been continuously enhanced, with many favorable conditions to maintain the long-term healthy and stable development of the economy, China's current economic development has also encountered outstanding contradictions and problems, and is taking measures to actively solve them.
"I believe that as long as we maintain our strategic focus, comprehensively deepen reform and opening up, and make every effort to solve the outstanding contradictions and problems, China's economy will surely be able to accelerate its transition to a high-quality development track," Xi Jinping said.
On November 3rd and 4th, the "A CLASSIC TOUR student and classic world tour" for two consecutive nights in Haikou Wuyuan River Culture and Sports Center, 86,000 spectators at the scene to see the "god of the song" Zhang Xueyou style, Haikou police organized more than 6,600 security forces to carry out the on-site and surrounding public security, traffic order maintenance work, two days, Haikou police arrested a total of "scaling cattle" 20 people, the sale of false documents.
During the concert, the Haikou City Public Security Bureau's main leaders on-site command and supervision of traffic, public security and other security work, various units, the police participating in the war to play the excellent style of continuous combat, two consecutive days in advance of 4 hours, solidly carry out anti-explosion security inspection, dredging traffic, order maintenance, service to the masses and other security work.
Due to the timely release of traffic travel tips in the early stage, reasonable division of the parking area, the timely guidance of the surrounding roads, after the end of the concert on the evening of 65 minutes, on the evening of the 4th it took only 55 minutes, a total of more than 86,000 spectators and more than 20,000 vehicles for two nights to leave in a safe and orderly manner.
The death toll from the earthquake and tsunami in Indonesia has risen to 420, and there have been no reports of casualties among Chinese citizens.
Indonesia's official Antara news agency at midnight local time on the morning of the 29th local time, citing the country's disaster relief agency head Wilem Rampangilei released the figures, the number of deaths caused by a strong earthquake and tsunami occurred in Indonesia's Central Sulawesi Province has risen to 420 people.
According to the official, this is only the statistics of Palu, the capital of the Central Sulawesi province, and does not include Donggala County and the nearby Sigi area, where the epicentre, because communication between the two areas is still interrupted and the number of victims has not yet been reported.
Because many roads in Palu have been severely damaged, heavy machinery is difficult to enter, and the search and rescue work has encountered great difficulties.
In order to protect the rescue, Palu Airport, which began to close on the evening of the 28th, stopped all commercial flights after reopening on the evening of the 29th, and the reporter's flight from Jakarta to Palu was cancelled that night.
After the earthquake and tsunami, the Chinese Embassy in Indonesia learned and verified the situation of Chinese citizens in the affected areas through various channels.
Up to now, there have been no reports of casualties among Chinese citizens.
“The supersonic project is being carried out in accordance with the contract signed with the Ministry of Industry and Trade,” said Serpalo, director of Russia’s Zhukovsky Central Aerofluid Dynamics Research Institute.
We think it will take two to three years for a technology demonstration, and another 10 to 15 years for civilian aircraft production.
Cerpalo said that the current problem for Russian scientists is how to balance the economy and safety of the aircraft.
Supersonic aircraft, he said, are characterised by huge noise effects.
Serpalo said that the institute is working with the Moscow Aeronautical Institute and the Tupolev Design Bureau to develop a full range of civil supersonic aircraft, including business jets and large passenger aircraft for commercial transportation.
General Secretary Xi Jinping delivered a very important speech at the private enterprise symposium, injecting firm confidence into the private economy towards a broader stage.
General Secretary Xi Jinping stressed that "let entrepreneurs take off the burden of thought and move forward lightly" has aroused strong resonance among the vast number of entrepreneurs and innovative entrepreneurs.
Market vitality comes from people, especially entrepreneurship, from entrepreneurship.
In the course of 40 years of reform and opening up, there have been stories of thousands of entrepreneurship and innovation of thousands of entrepreneurs, and the growth and growth of the entrepreneurial group has continuously promoted the breakthrough of China's economy.
For a period of time, some people in the society have made some negations and doubts about the private economy.
The so-called â€œPrivate economy departure theoryâ€ and â€œnew public-private partnership theoryâ€ have aroused the doubts and concerns of some entrepreneurs.
Recently, some private enterprises have encountered a lot of difficulties and problems in business development.
For example, the changes in the international economic environment have an impact on some export enterprises; the rapid adjustment of the demand structure has led to the pressure of transformation and upgrading; some policies are uncoordinated with each other, the policy effects are superimposed, or the working methods are simple, resulting in the opposite effect of some policies with good intentions.
A variety of factors are intertwined, the private economy is encountering difficulties, some private enterprises are facing difficulties, and entrepreneurs show a lot of anxiety.
In this context, to correct the misunderstanding of the understanding, remove the ideological burden of entrepreneurs, let the enterprise single-mindedly strive for development, the government single-minded to promote development, which is related to market confidence and development expectations, and has a particularly profound practical significance.
At the symposium, the important judgment of the "three unalterable changes" was re-emphasized: "The status and role of the non-public economy in China's economic and social development have not changed!"
From the in-depth promotion of decentralization, the establishment of a power list system to create a rule of law environment to protect the legitimate rights and interests of entrepreneurs, to create a market environment of fair competition, shaping the atmosphere of respect for entrepreneurs in the whole society, in recent years, the Party Central Committee has paid unprecedented importance to entrepreneurs and institutional protection.
The symposium clearly put forward policies and measures to strongly support the development and growth of private enterprises in six aspects, and launched a series of pragmatic actions that are committed to private enterprises.
All of this has given great encouragement to the group of entrepreneurs and given more expectations from all sectors of society.
The fog is gone, the policy has been decided, and the key is to implement it.
It is necessary to continuously create a better development environment for the private economy, help private enterprises to solve the difficulties in development, and help realize China's economic transformation and upgrading; to let entrepreneurs feel fair in the market competition, feel safe in legitimate business, feel respected in social life, and stimulate innovative vitality and creative potential.
China's economy has entered the process of moving towards high-quality development, which requires more entrepreneurs to exercise their ambitions, and also provides a greater space and stage for entrepreneurs to exert their creativity.
We have reason to believe that with the further deepening of reform and the removal of obstacles, the private economy will usher in better development prospects and development opportunities and move towards a broader stage.
Inner Mongolia import and export links 46 kinds of supervision certificates all to achieve network verification - Sino-Singapore network
November 5 (Reporter Li Aiping) Hohhot customs said on the 5th that from now on, in addition to special circumstances such as confidentiality needs, 46 kinds of supervision certificates in the local import and export links have been networked for verification.
Enterprises in Inner Mongolia can declare the relevant documents to the customs in a paper-free way, avoiding problems such as on-the-site rush, paper applications, and repeated submissions in the past.
It is understood that the document preparation time refers to the preparation time of various types of documents required for the import and export link before the customs declaration, which is one of the main factors that affect the overall customs clearance time, in order to compress the customs clearance time and reduce the customs clearance cost, it is necessary to reduce the documents.
Previously, 86 kinds of various regulatory documents needed for customs verification in the import and export links, involving 19 departments.
It is reported that in accordance with the principle of "cancellation of cancellations, mergers that can be combined, can withdraw from port verification", relying on the "single window" platform of international trade, the customs and other 16 certification authorities system docking and data interconnection, to achieve more data running, enterprises less errands.
Customs said that in the past, enterprises needed to go back and forth to the on-site office hall of the relevant departments to submit paper applications, and the process was lengthy and could not track the audit status in real-time.
At present, enterprise users can directly log in to the "single window" portal to make online applications.
After the approval of the certification department, the electronic data of the certificate will be transmitted to the customs, and the automatic comparison and intelligent verification of the customs declaration data will be realized during the customs clearance process, and the audit results will be unified through the "single window" feedback to the enterprise, and the whole process of regulatory document declaration, audit, customs clearance and feedback will be handled online.
The export of Korean chicken soup to China has soared 20 times in four years, or it is related to the increase in the number of young people in the empty nest
The export of chicken soup to China has soared 20 times in the past four years analysis: it is related to the increase in the number of empty nest young people
Yonhap News Agency reported on the 5th that the export value of South Korean chicken soup to China last year exceeded 100,000 US dollars, a sharp increase of about 20 times compared with 2013 four years ago.
According to the analysis, this increase is related to the increase in the number of empty-nesting young people in China, which drives the popularity of convenient food, as well as young people's focus on nutritious meals.
The data was released by the Korean Agricultural and Aquatic Food Circulation Corporation (aT) on the 5th.
Last year, South Korea's chicken soup exports to China amounted to 10.0339 million U.S. dollars, weighing 218.59 million kilograms, a sharp increase of 2094% and 3668.8 percent compared with 2013.
According to the analysis, the increase in the sales of chicken soup in South Korea in China is related to the increase in the number of empty-nest young people driving the hot sales of convenience food, as well as young people's attention to nutritious meals.
As of this year, China's one-person family has exceeded the 200 million mark and is expected to increase to 30% of the total population in 2020, and local food companies have also launched a variety of convenient food for the "single family".
In addition, the analysis also pointed out that avian influenza is the biggest factor hindering chicken soup from taking root in the mainland Chinese market.
AT said that from November 2016 to April last year, there was an avian influenza epidemic in South Korea, and the relevant departments completely banned the export of chicken soup to China, resulting in a sharp reduction in exports.
In 2016, chicken soup exports to China amounted to 840,000 U.S. dollars, due to avian influenza, exports plummeted to $100,000 last year.
The first high-quality development forum of Anhui listed companies and Anhui listed company report conference was held in Hefei on the 30th.
Deng Xiangyang, standing deputy governor of the Anhui Provincial Party Committee, said that this forum aims to build a comprehensive exchange platform for cross-border integration and industrial and financial integration, which is of great practical significance to promote the healthy growth of listed companies in Anhui, promote the construction of the capital market, and build an innovative and modern industrial system.
Anhui will further strengthen the company's listed reserve resources, promote the organic combination of Anhui's leading industries, emerging industries and the capital market, actively cultivate listed resources, and give full play to the "leading" role of listed companies in leading industrial upgrading and cultivating new drivers of economic development.
Chen Xiang said that to promote Anhui's economic transformation and upgrading and to achieve high-quality development, there is an urgent need for Anhui listed companies to improve quality and efficiency and play a leading role.
I hope to use this forum as a starting point to build a co-construction, sharing and sharing platform for the integration of "political, industrial, academic and research funds", and form a strategic alliance around listed companies and an "investment + investment bank" capital ecosystem.
The provincial capital of Hefei is definitely ahead of other cities in the province with the number of 45 listed companies.
In terms of industry distribution, Anhui listed companies cover 13 industry categories, nearly 70% are concentrated in the manufacturing industry, and the proportion of listed companies in strategic emerging industries and high-tech industries is low.
The largest anime festival in South America takes place in Lima, the capital of Peru.
The four-day event, organized by local anime fans in Peru, is expected to reach 100,000 visitors.
According to Japan's NHK TV reported on November 5th, the content of the anime festival is rich and colorful, including American anime character display, popular Japanese anime "Seven Dragon Ball" Spanish voice actor's talk show, Japanese anime theme song karaoke contest, anime role-playing competition, etc., wonderful.
The excitement of the meeting is extraordinary.
In the anime role-playing competition, some of the children dressed up the characters of popular Japanese anime, and reproduced the scene when these characters debuted, and the wonderful performance won the enthusiastic applause of the audience.
Peru's cable TV channels and so on from two years ago continue to broadcast Japanese anime works, which allows more and more local people to like Japanese anime, some couples even gave their newborn baby anime character names, the huge impact of Japanese anime culture can be seen.
Repair arrangements damaged by typhoon balconstruction facilities at the entrance of Comes China-Portuguese middle school
Recently, some members of the public have paid attention to the repair arrangements caused by the damage caused by the "mangosteen" attack on some of the facilities at the entrance of the Chinese and Portuguese secondary schools, and this bureau has been paying close attention to and following up.
After the "mangosteen" attack, the school has immediately contacted and arranged engineering maintenance companies for follow-up.
After inspection by the engineering personnel, it was determined that the damaged part of the gate was still stable and did not affect the use of the entrance.
In order to repair the damaged part as soon as possible, the school has immediately launched the award process for the repair project, which will be carried out sequentially this week.
At the same time, the school has arranged an emergency engineering maintenance company to carry out the necessary interim measures to ensure the safety of the campus environment.
On September 29, the first HSK study abroad employment exhibition in the Philippines was opened at the Guangqi School in Manila, the capital of the Philippines. Thirteen well-known Chinese colleges and universities such as Tsinghua University jointly enrolled in the Philippines for the first time, and 7 Chinese-funded enterprises such as China Power Construction and China International Airlines recruited staff on the spot in the Philippines.
On the 29th, the first HSK study abroad employment exhibition in the Philippines was opened, 13 well-known Chinese colleges and universities such as Tsinghua University were recruited in the Philippines for the first time, and seven Chinese-funded enterprises such as China Power Construction and China International Airlines recruited staff on the spot in the Philippines.
Tsai Art, vice chairman of the Philippine Chinese Education Center, said that since its establishment in 1994, it has hosted a total of 29 Chinese proficiency tests and 4 Chinese proficiency oral examinations, with a total of 47,000 people participating in the exam.
In order to enable the vast number of Chinese language learners in the Philippines to become successful and useful, this year, under the guidance of the Confucius Institute Headquarters/National Hankanto Hanko International, the first HSK study abroad employment exhibition was held.
The first HSK study and employment exhibition in the Philippines, China's colleges and universities are burning at the admissions site.
Liu Xiaolong, manager of the international examination department of the Confucius Institute headquarters/Hanban Hankue, said that in 2017, more than 25,000 people participated in the HSK exam in the Philippines, and the Philippines has become one of the countries with the largest number of HSK test takers.
It is hoped that Philippine Chinese language learners will have the opportunity to communicate face-to-face with China's first-class university teachers, and at the same time expand the source of overseas students from well-known Chinese colleges and universities in China; invite Chinese-funded enterprises in the Philippines to participate in the exhibition, hoping to provide employment options for international students who come to China after graduation.
TOLENTINO AQUINO, deputy director of the Education Bureau of the Capital of the Philippines, said in his speech that public schools in the Manila area have opened more Chinese language courses, and as Philippine-Chinese relations have entered the best period in history, Chinese language has become a very useful skill, and China's well-known institutions of higher learning will promote educational cooperation between the two countries.
Participated in the same day's Chinese proficiency test, there were 1304 candidates from 10 schools in the Greater Manila area and 25 social test takers, who applied for the HSK level 2 to 6.
Teacher Liu Yuting, the admissions office of Tsinghua University, told the China News Agency that many Filipino students were prepared to show interest in Tsinghua's economic management, computer and medical majors.
He pointed out that Filipino students with HSK scores of more than 5 can log on to the school's official website for online application.
China News Agency reporters at the booth of the Southwest University of Finance and Economics saw that less than ten o'clock, there have been 14 students left the intention to apply.
Teacher Bai Qiaoyan, who is in charge of enrollment, has six kinds of scholarships for overseas students, including the highest Chinese national government scholarship (doctoral category), free to pay tuition fees, provide accommodation, with monthly living expenses of 3,500 yuan.
Qin Shanghai, dean of the School of International Education of Ocean University of China, told reporters that marine science, marine life, marine geology, aquaculture and the utilization of marine living resources are the characteristic disciplines of the university.
China has a very long coastline, the Philippines is an island country, and marine scientific research has needs and can complement each other.
Tongji University has several majors in the world, including civil engineering, ocean, management and other majors and the Philippines demand docking.
At present, there are four Filipino students studying at the school.
The on-site recruitment of Chinese-funded enterprises are well-known enterprises that have been cultivated in the Philippines for many years.
Southern Airlines received three resumes on the same day.
The positions recruited by the Philippine representative office of China Power Construction include company clerks, power plant on-site management, power plant construction engineers and so on.
"It is hoped that Filipino students will go to China to study in a targeted manner, such as studying China's electric welding technology and coming back to participate in the country's 'Jianjian special construction' plan, and the employment opportunities will be very good," said Zhao Changjie of the representative office.
U.S. warship approaches China's South China Sea islands and reefs
U.S. Navy destroyer U.S. Navy destroyer USS Decatur has sailed into waters near Beijing’s claimed South China Sea island on the eve of China’s 11th National Day.
According to U.S. officials requesting anonymity, the U.S. destroyer USS Decatur sailed within 12 nautical miles of Gaven Reef and Johnson Reef in the Spratly Islands.
The official said the U.S. conducts regular free-navigation missions and, as it has done in the past, it will continue to do so in the future.
U.S. President Donald Trump accuses Beijing of trying to interfere in U.S. congressional elections and entering a new phase of pressurizing Beijing on behalf of Washington.
Prior to this, the U.S. Navy also had two U.S. Navy warships entering the waters near islands claimed by China in the South China Sea.
According to comments from Washington, the move is likely to irritate China at a time of tension between the United States and the United States.
WASHINGTON, Nov 5 (Reuters) - U.S. sanctions on Iran’s oil and financial sector on Monday stepped up efforts to limit Iran’s missile and nuclear programs and curb Iran’s growing military and political influence in the Middle East.
Such a move would reinstate U.S. sanctions lifted under the 2015 Iran nuclear deal and add 300 additional sanctions on Iran’s oil, shipping, insurance and banking sectors.
The details of the sanctions will be released by Secretary of State Mike Pompeo and Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin at the 1330 GMT press conference.
The U.S. has said it will temporarily allow the continued purchase of Iranian oil from eight importers, including major buyers of Iranian oil such as China, India, South Korea, Japan and Turkey, to ensure that crude prices remain stable.
U.S. officials have said the countries will put money paid to Iran in a escrow account.
A few days ago, the General Office of the Ministry of Education issued a notice on the progress of the rectification of special governance actions for out-of-school training institutions nationwide. As of October 15, 2018, there were 400,532 out-of-campus training institutions in the country, 272,175 institutions with problems, and 83,510 rectification and rectification rates have been completed, with a rectification rate of 30.68%.
There are 6,611 institutions in Heilongjiang Province that have identified 2,178, and the rectification rate has reached 32.95%.
It is reported that at present, China's out-of-school training institutions special governance work has entered a comprehensive rectification stage, in accordance with the spirit issued by the General Office of the "Opinions on standardizing the development of out-of-university training institutions", in order to effectively do a good job in the special governance rectification of out-of-school training institutions, to ensure the completion of rectification tasks by the end of the year, the provincial education administrative departments in accordance with the detailed investigation and preliminary rectification.
In accordance with the setting standards or rectification and acceptance qualified into the white list, and announced to the public in a timely manner.
In order to prevent misleading parents and students and prevent excessive training and false propaganda, it should be based on the principles of simplicity, intuitiveity, accuracy and standardization, according to the student's grade and participating disciplines, naming the name of the discipline training courses, and the training institutions should report the name, training content, enrollment object, schedule and class time of the training courses to the county-level education department as soon as possible.
Classes that have not passed the filing audit shall not be subject to enrollment training.
Teachers who have strictly mastered the qualifications of teachers engaged in language, mathematics, English and physics, chemistry, biology and other subject knowledge training should have the corresponding teacher qualifications.
The Fujian provincial flood control office reported on the 30th, in view of this year's No. 24 Typhoon "Tammei" on Fujian's coastal and maritime areas has basically ended, according to the "Fujian provincial flood control typhoon emergency plan", at 10 o'clock on the 30th to terminate the typhoon emergency response, all relevant areas can return to normal production and life order in a timely manner.
Typhoon "Tanmei" began to turn at noon on the 29th, moving along the northeast, gradually moving away from Fujian Province, at 8 o'clock on the 30th Typhoon Center is located about 140 kilometers to the east of Kagoshima, Japan.
As a result, the Fujian Provincial Meteorological Observatory at 8 o'clock on the 30th to lift the "sea wind warning level III".
Previously, in order to prevent Typhoon Tanmei, as of 11 o'clock on the 28th, Fujian has evacuated 268 fishing boats and transferred 2,282 elderly and young people.
Sino-Vietnamese border estuary port held a national gate flag-raising ceremony to celebrate the National Day
"I can't believe that there is such a magnificent flag-raising ceremony on the frontier, which is even more shocking than watching the flag raising in the mainland."
On the morning of the 1st, Mr. Zhang, who came from Sichuan for tourism at the Yunnan Estuary on the Sino-Vietnamese border, and more than 500 army officers and soldiers, residents and Chinese and foreign tourists jointly watched the flag-raising ceremony to celebrate the 69th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China and celebrated the 69th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China.
The estuary port is the largest port in the Yunnan section of the Sino-Vietnamese border and is located in Hekou County, Red River Prefecture in Yunnan Province, across the river from the old street city of Vietnam, and belongs to a national type of port.
With the continuous deepening of the country's "Belt and Road" construction, as one of China's most convenient channels for connecting Southeast Asia, the flow of estuary ports of entry and exit has grown steadily.
At 7:30 a.m. on the same day, the sun had just revealed a corner, and the limited area of the estuary at the estuary of the estuary at the estuary had gathered early to watch the flag-raising ceremony with local people and Chinese and foreign tourists.
At 7:45 p.m., the flag-raising ceremony began punctually, and the members of the national honor guard at the estuary border checkpoint were shivering in spirit and escorted the national flag to the flag-raising platform at a healthy pace.
After the commander's order to raise the flag, the flag bearer waving his arms and drew an arc, and the bright five-star red flag, like an "Eagle spreads its wings", slowly raised with the motivating melody of the national anthem.
"In each New Year's Day, the Spring Festival, the National Day and other important time nodes to hold the National Day flag-raising ceremony, not only to show the image of China, but also to stimulate the patriotic feelings of the people of all ethnic groups in the border."
The honor guard officers who participated in the flag-raising ceremony said.
It is reported that the national honor guard in charge of the flag-raising ceremony at Hekou Port consists of more than 40 officers and soldiers from various positions at the estuary border checkpoint, ranging from a three-person flag-raising team to a large-scale honor guard, which has experienced more than 60 years of history, and has carried out more than 70 national-level foreign affairs activities since its formation.
The newly revised personal income tax law adjusts China's personal income tax resident assessment standards from one full year to 183 days.
On the 30th, the relevant person in charge of China's Ministry of Finance and the State Administration of Taxation said that in order to maintain the stability of the policy, the next step in the implementation of the new personal income tax law will consider continuing to make preferential arrangements for foreigners, including Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan.
The person in charge said that the implementation regulations of the current personal income tax law have special preferential provisions on the payment of taxes by foreigners, and individuals who do not have a residence in China but have lived for more than one year or less live for more than one or five years can only pay personal income tax based on the part paid by units or individuals in mainland China.
The amount paid abroad does not need to pay personal income tax within the territory of China.
The Ministry of Finance of China, the State Administration of Taxation, the National Development and Reform Commission and the Ministry of Commerce have also issued a notice to expand the scope of application of foreign investors to distribut direct investment withholding income.
For the profits distributed by foreign investors from resident enterprises within the territory of China, the scope of application of the withholding income tax policy shall be extended to all non-prohibited foreign-invested projects to all non-prohibited foreign-invested projects and fields.
On the sidelines of the 73rd session of the United Nations General Assembly, various parties released some positive information on the Korean Peninsula issue.
South Korean President Moon Jae-in relayed North Korea’s “irreversible” determination to denuclearize and said U.S. President Donald Trump and North Korea’s supreme leader Kim Jong Un could meet by the end of the year.
The U.S. State Department later said that Secretary of State Mike Pompeo will visit North Korea in October to promote the implementation of the U.S. and North Korean leaders' commitments to meet in Singapore.
Since the beginning of this year's beginning of this year, the DPRK and the ROK have opened the road to dialogue, the leaders of the DPRK and the ROK and the United States have held meetings, the general trend of de-escalation of the situation on the Korean Peninsula has continued, and the principle of resolving the Korean Peninsula issue has also been adhered to.
First of all, there has been no change in the fact that "the essence of the Korean Peninsula issue is the issue of security problems". The key to achieving peace on the Korean Peninsula is to properly and balancedly resolve the legitimate security concerns of all parties, rather than blindly exerting pressure on the other side and blindly emphasizing their own demands.
Secondly, in the dialogue to realize the denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula, the relevant parties on the steps and methods to achieve the denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula are still divided, and due to the long-term lack of political trust between the DPRK and the United States, the game thinking of "who comes first and then" is still strong.
A few days ago, at the Security Council's public meeting on the Korean Peninsula issue held at the United Nations headquarters in New York, the different voices issued by various parties on the issue of sanctions against the DPRK once again highlighted that these two points on the Korean Peninsula issue have not changed.
U.S. Secretary of State Mike Pompeo insisted that sanctions on North Korea would not be lifted until the Korean Peninsula was fully denuclearized.
Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov, on the other hand, emphasized the principle of “responding by action” and pointed out that "the weakening trend of sanctions should take the same pace as North Korea's steps on the path of gradual abandonment of nuclear weapons."
Undoubtedly, the relevant parties should continue to fully, completely and accurately implement the DPRK-related resolutions of the Security Council, but pressure is not the goal, the implementation of sanctions and the promotion of a political settlement are the requirements of the Security Council resolutions, the two can not be scrapped, can not choose only one.
As Chinese State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said, in view of the current positive developments in inter-Korean and DPRK-US relations, China believes that it is necessary for the Security Council to consider the timely initiation of reversible provisions, so as to encourage the DPRK and relevant parties to take greater steps in the direction of denuclearization.
In retrospect, the denuclearization of the denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula and every advance in the peace process requires all parties to show sufficient political courage.
At present, in the face of the increasingly high expectations of the international community to promote the political settlement of the Korean Peninsula issue, the relevant parties in particular should show their political strength and make political decisions, implement their commitments and solve difficult problems, continue to take steps to meet each other, advance the denuclearization of the Korean Peninsula and the establishment of a peace mechanism on the Korean Peninsula, and jointly create a permanent peace on the Korean Peninsula.
The people's government of Ji County, Linfen City, Shanxi Province, said on the 1st that during the National People's Day, the Yellow River Kekou Waterfall Scenic Area located in the county will maintain a relatively high water level and do not have open conditions.
In order to ensure safety, scenic spots are temporarily closed during the National Day.
The Yellow River Kekou Falls is the second largest waterfall in China and the world's largest yellow waterfall.
The Yellow River runs to this point, the stones on both sides stand on both sides, and the estuary is as narrow as a pot mouth, forming the atmosphere of "a thousand miles of the Yellow River a pot".
According to the reporter's understanding, every year from June to October is the flood season of the Yellow River, starting from July 12, 2018, due to the high water level of the Yellow River, Shanxi Yellow River Kekou Scenic Area has begun to be closed one after another.
Ni Yufeng, chief engineer of Hukou Scenic Area Management Committee, told the media that this is the longest in the past 20 years, the Yellow River's high-water level continued for the longest time, "There has not been so long, in 2017, our flood season closure time is 4 days, this year is nearly a month."
It is understood that in order to meet the â€œEleventhâ€ Golden Week, the scenic area of Shanxi Yellow River Kekou Waterfall originally increased personnel arrangements and vehicle maintenance in advance, as well as the recruitment of temporary staff, etc., have been put in place.
According to the "notice on doing a good job of the Yellow River flood control work during the National Day" issued by the "Yellow River Flood Prevention and Drought Control General Command Office", Qinghai, Gansu, Ningxia, Inner Mongolia, Shanxi, Shaanxi, Henan and Shandong Province are required to do a good job in the flood control of the Yellow River during the National Day.
At present, there is a large flow of dry rivers in the Yangtze River, the flow rate of upstream rivers is maintained at 2000-3000 cubic meters per second, the flow rate of midstream rivers is maintained at 2500-3500 cubic meters per second, and the downstream river flow is maintained at 3000 cubic meters per second.
Influenza vaccination services provided by health centres and health stations especially on the National Day holiday
The Health Bureau ordered 150,000 doses of the 2018-2019 quadrivalent influenza vaccine this year, at this stage to give priority to high-risk people free of charge, in order to facilitate the vaccination of residents during the holidays, health centers and health stations under the Health Bureau, especially during the National Day holiday (October 1 and 2) to provide vaccination services.
In addition to the above-mentioned convenience measures, the health centers and health stations under the Health Bureau have extended the influenza vaccination service from Monday to Friday until 8 p.m., and as of 4 p.m. on September 30, 4,158 people have been vaccinated, compared with more than 3,714 in the same period last year.
Vaccinations are available free of charge to the following Macao residents: persons between the ages of 6 months and 18 years of age, persons aged 50 and above, pregnant women, all persons with chronic diseases, including obese persons (i.e. those with a BMI of 30 or above), as well as staff in institutions, nurseries, kindergartens, primary and secondary schools, all health workers, as well as Macao residents who work in gambling and casinos.
At the same time, the Health Bureau will take the initiative to contact the relevant agencies for other personnel who deem it necessary to vaccinate, including the public sector, to contact the relevant agencies to arrange vaccination by the health center.
In order to facilitate vaccinators and reduce vaccination time, the Health Bureau will send medical staff to local secondary schools, primary schools, kindergartens and nurseries from October to December this year to vaccinate young children, primary and secondary school students, teachers and employees for collective influenza vaccination; in addition, the Health Bureau will also arrange for personnel to vaccinate the elderly and handicapped institutions, a large number of public departments or other institutions.
Students and young children who are unable to participate in group vaccinations may be vaccinated with the Macao Resident Identity Card, the Health Bureau user card, the Influenza Vaccination Vaccination Card (if any), the student ID card, the Employee's ID card or the career certificate vaccinated at the Count Ren General Hospital Vaccination Centre from December 3, 2018.
From September 2017 to August 2018, those who have received the 2017-2018 influenza vaccine still need to be vaccinated with the new influenza vaccine from September 2018, because the influenza antigen content contained in the 2018-2019 Northern Hemisphere influenza vaccine has been updated, and it is aimed at seasonal influenza in the northern hemisphere in the 2018-2019 winter and summer of 2019.
Macao's influenza peak generally occurs from January to March of each year, later than in temperate areas (such as northern China and Japan), and the Health Bureau calls on the elderly, children, pregnant women, obese people and people with chronic diseases and other high-risk people who are more prone to complications, and those who are in regular contact with high-risk people should be vaccinated as soon as possible.
Nov. 30 (Xinhua) -- The NBA's reigning champion's Warriors battle with the Timberwolves at home this morning, and Roer Deng, who joined the Timberwolves in the summer, helped the team take a victory from the road with a key make-up.
In the first quarter, the Timberwolves took the lead in winning the ball, and Ross hit the first goal of the game.
The Warriors Jones responded.
Subsequently, Curry Durant made a long shot, and Ross and Tigg also felt hot, and the two sides began to fight each other.
At the end of the first quarter, the Warrior 36:37 Timberwolves.
In the second quarter, the rotation team debuted, and the shooting rate of the two teams decreased.
The Warriors scored super goals with a few baskets.
Later, they played a wave of 8:1 small climax to open the score.
The Timberwolves rely on the scores of Tigue and Downes.
At half-time, the Warriors 71:65 The Timberwolves.
It is easy to fight again, and the warriors stop the Timberwolves in a wave of 5:0.
Suspension returned, and the Warriors have maintained a very strong lead.
In the second half of the second half of the third quarter, the Timberwolves began to pursue points.
After a small climax of 16:3, the Timberwolves 94:92 ended the third quarter.
In the fourth quarter of the game, the Timberwolves came up with a wave of 6:0 to open the score gap, and Warrior Derrickson hit two and three points to help the team stop the decline.
In the run-off stage, the Timberwolves new aid Roer Dunlian took 6 points and hit the key basket, and in the end, the Timberwolves defeated the Warriors in 114:110.
In terms of data, Curry played 20 minutes with 21 points and 4 assists, Thompson's three-point 4 of 3 points scored 17 points, Durant's 16 points, Derrickson substituted 10 points.
The Timberwolves scored a double-double by six, with Tigue with 17 points, Ross with 16 points, Tolive with 15, Downs with 12 and Wiggins with 11.
On the evening of September 29, the reporter learned from the Propaganda Department of the Qingbaijiang District Party Committee of Chengdu that on the evening of September 29, Beijing time, a train full of automotive connectors, telescopes, liquid crystal displays and other goods (Chengdu) was reinstalled through the Shemyanułka port in Poland, and finally arrived in Nuremberg, Germany.
This is the first time that the China-Europe train has opened the Polish Shemyanułka port route, marking the successful opening of another European transport route after the China-Europe train, following Mara and Chopp.
The China-Europe train is listed on September 14th from Chengdu Qingbaijiang Castle Station, exited through Alashankou, entered Europe through the Shemyanuvka Port in Poland, and finally arrived in Nuremberg, Germany, for a total of about 16 days.
For the first time, the China-Europe train will carry out the replacement operation of the wide track and the standard rail here.
The opening of this port has effectively solved the long-term operation and long-term problems caused by the congestion at the Mala port, improved the timeliness of train transportation, and provided a new solution to the congestion problem of the Mala port, further improved the carrying capacity and transportation efficiency of the western hinterland of China to the European Mediterranean market, and laid a solid foundation for the development of the European market.
A 7.5-magnitude earthquake struck the Indonesian island of Sulawesi on Friday, and more than 400 people have been confirmed to have died, many of whom have been swept away by tsunami waves caused by the earthquake.
The total number of deaths on Sunday is expected to increase significantly as new figures are reported in remote areas.
Dozens of people were reportedly still trapped under the rubble of a hotel and a shopping mall in the city of Baru.
Large waves as high as six meters (20 feet) caused by the earthquake hit the city of Baru.
So far there has been only the death toll from Baru, the death toll in Dungra in the northern part of Baru has been reported very slowly, and authorities are preparing for an even worse situation.
Dungra has a living population of 300,000, which is closer to the epicentre of the earthquake.
Indonesia's vice-presidency said the death toll could rise to thousands.
Hundreds of people gathered at the beach to celebrate the festival as the twilight waves hit the coast at dusk on Friday, and many people were swept away by the huge waves, and everything was destroyed wherever they went.
TOKYO, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Confidence among Japan’s biggest manufacturers hit their lowest level in more than a year in the September quarter, according to the Bank of Japan’s quarterly survey released on Monday, as rising raw material costs and a series of natural disasters affect production put pressure on companies.
The survey barely shows that escalating global trade frictions have dampened the confidence of large manufacturers.
However, the risk of an all-out trade war has hit the company's business prospects and may threaten corporate capital expenditures.
Aggressive capital spending is a bright spot in Japan’s economy.
The survey called into question the Bank of Japan’s view that a robust economic expansion would help accelerate inflation toward its 2 percent target, although there are signs that companies are gradually transferring costs to customers.
â€œManufacturer confidence is stagnating due to slowing exports and weak factory production amid concerns caused by the global trade war,â€ said Nan Wuzhi, principal researcher at the Joint Research Institute of Agriculture and Forestry.
â€œConfidence is still high. And because corporate earnings are improving and prices are rising, I don't think it's going to continue to decline."
According to the short-term survey, the large-scale manufacturing prosperity judgment index in September fell from positive 21 three months ago to positive 19, worsening for the third consecutive quarter.
The median estimate for the market is positive 22.
The large non-manufacturing economic judgment index in September fell to positive 22 from 24 in the June survey, deteriorating for the first time in eight quarters.
A Reuters poll is 22.
According to the survey, the large-scale manufacturing and non-manufacturing economic judgment indicators are expected to remain stable in December.
Investors don't care about the decline in the short-term business climate judgment index, the Nikkei .N225 rose to a 27-year-old high on Monday, as the continued depreciation of the yen helped to improve the export earnings prospects of Japanese companies.
Capital expenditures are robust.
Despite a decline in business confidence, the latest short-term outlook highlights the solidity of corporate capital spending plans, driven by renewed capacity and increased investment in robotics and automation to cope with labor shortages caused by an aging population.
According to the central bank's short-term survey, large enterprises plan to increase capital expenditure by 13.4% in the current fiscal year ending in March 2019.
It was 13.6% in the previous short-term observation survey.
All corporate capital spending is expected to grow by 8.5 percent this fiscal year, near the pace of Japan's bubble economy.
â€œThere is still room for further growth in capital spending, given that small businesses have raised their profit estimates from now on, but this will largely depend on the impact of the trade war on corporate confidence,â€ he said.
The increased ability of firms to pass-on costs, with the large-scale output-to-earnings price index at a positive seven-decade high, is an encouraging sign that Japan’s efforts to combat deflation have made progress.
The index, which measures the employment situation of large enterprises, hit minus 23, the tightest level since 1992, underscoring the tightening labor market.
Benefiting from strong corporate spending, Japan's economy rebounded in the second quarter of this year's contraction from January to March this year.
However, escalated trade frictions in the summer and the disruption of the supply chain due to natural disasters have clouded Japan’s export-dependent economic prospects.
In U.S. dollars, the growth rate of import and export of services is 16.4%.
The press release of the website of the Ministry of Commerce quoted the person in charge of the Department of Service and Trade as saying that the total import and export of emerging services from January to August exceeded 1 trillion yuan, and the growth rate was faster than the overall increase.
Among them, the total import and export of emerging services is 1,138.39 billion yuan, an increase of 20.9%, 10.4 percentage points higher than the overall growth rate of service imports and exports, and the proportion of emerging services has increased by nearly 3 percentage points.
In terms of service exports, from January to August, service exports continued the rapid growth momentum of this year, and the export growth rate was 5.7 percentage points higher than the growth rate of imports.
Among them, the top three growth areas are telecommunications computer and information services, personal culture and entertainment services, and insurance services, with a growth rate of 61.1%, 38.8% and 26.5% respectively.
The person in charge of the Service and Trade Department also pointed out that the proportion of emerging service imports from January to August has also gradually increased.
From January to August, the import of emerging services grew rapidly, accounting for 23.6% of service imports, an increase of 1.6 percentage points over the same period last year.
Among them, the import growth rate of financial services, intellectual property royalties, telecommunications computers and information services is more than 20%, 47.1%, 23.3% and 23.2% respectively.
La Liga: Macy's substitute assists to equal the Barca's three-round insurrected.
